      "message": "nit: why add these functions here, before any other functions? Are they more important than anything else?\n\nIn this `mmu.c` file we tend to: 1. put all static function definitions before all non-static ones. 2. when adding a new static or non-static function, add it at the end after all other static or non-static functions (unless there is a particular reason to put it elsewhere). So, put `iommu_tlb_flush()` after `need_memcache_topup()`, and `(pkvm_)register_iommu_tlb_flush()` after `pkvm_host_unuse_dma()`?",
